      "side": 1,
      "message": "Alternatively (and probably even better, honestly) would be to fix our non-hex path dumping code to print floats such that they round-trip. I\u0027m pretty sure that\u0027s as simple as changing this line:\n\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/core/SkStringUtils.cpp;l\u003d19;drc\u003d57665886a1bb4533871c9b28f1e6b977755457e3\n\n... so that it uses \"%.9g\" rather than \"%g\". Justification:\n\nhttps://randomascii.wordpress.com/2013/02/07/float-precision-revisited-nine-digit-float-portability/",
